1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,800
Do you say, "I am agree," "She don't like it," or "I didn't went"?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,200
These mistakes are more common than you think.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,400
In the next few minutes, you'll learn five simple corrections

4
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,600
that can make your English sound much more natural.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,000
And number five is a mistake you might make every day!

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:18,200
Meet Alex. Alex knows lots of English words,

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,600
but he keeps making five small grammar mistakes.

8
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:26,600
His friend Maya thinks she can catch them all.

9
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:30,200
Can you spot the mistakes before Maya does?

10
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,000
Let's find out.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Alex: I am agree with you!

12
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:42,600
Maya: Wait! Just say, "I agree with you."

13
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:47,400
Agree is already a verb. We don't need "am" before it.

14
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,600
Which is correct: "I agree" or "I am agree"?

15
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:56,000
It's "I agree." No "am."

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Alex: She don't play football.

17
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:27,600
Maya: She doesn't play football!

18
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:33,000
With he, she, and it, we use "doesn't" in the present simple negative.

19
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,600
He doesn't run. It doesn't work.

20
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:38,400
Alex: She don't... wait — She doesn't play football!

21
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
"I didn't went" is wrong.

22
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:14,000
After "didn't," use the base form of the verb.

23
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:19,000
Go, eat, see — not went, ate, saw.

24
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:23,600
Mini-quiz: "I didn't ___ breakfast." Eat or ate?

25
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:27,000
Three... two... one...

26
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:31,600
"I didn't eat breakfast." The base form is "eat."

27
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,000
"I have 25 years" is wrong.

28
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:58,400
We talk about age with "be," not "have."

29
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:02,000
"I am 25 years old." "She is 30."

30
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
"He go to school every day" is wrong.

31
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:44,000
In the present simple, add -s or -es to most verbs with he, she, or it.

32
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:47,200
She works. He watches TV. It rains.

33
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:51,400
Help Alex: "He ___ to school every day."

34
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:56,000
He goes to school every day!

35
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,400
Rapid-fire! Correct each sentence. Three... two... one...

36
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:31,600
"She don't understand."

37
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:34,400
She doesn't understand.

38
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:37,600
"I didn't saw him."

39
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:40,400
I didn't see him.

40
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:43,600
"He play football every day."

41
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:47,000
He plays football every day.

42
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:52,000
How many did you get? Share your score!

43
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:20,000
How many did you get right — three, four, or all five?

44
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:24,000
Tell me your score in the comments!

45
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:29,000
If you want to learn English grammar through simple animated stories,

46
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:33,200
subscribe and join us for the next lesson.

47
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:38,000
Making mistakes is part of learning. Keep practising!

48
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:40,000
Next: "Say These 10 English Sentences Correctly!"
